        <h2 id="s1">1. About these Terms</h2>
        <p>These Terms of Use ("Terms") apply to Matdo Grade for iPhone and iPad and its grading service, provided by Matdo Lab LLC ("we", "us"). By downloading, installing or using the app, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use it.</p>
        <p>You must be at least 18 to use the grading service. The App is intended for adult teachers, tutors and parents. Do not give anyone under 18 access to the grading service, including through a shared device.</p>
        <p>If you use the app on behalf of a school, tutoring center or other organization, you confirm that you have authority to agree for that organization. In that case, "you" includes both you and the organization.</p>
        <p>Our Privacy Policy explains how we handle information and forms part of these Terms. It is available in the app and at <a href="https://matdolab.com/privacy/grade">matdolab.com/privacy/grade</a>. The current Terms are also available at <a href="https://matdolab.com/terms/grade">matdolab.com/terms/grade</a>.</p>
        <h2 id="s2">2. Key points</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Matdo Grade uses AI to help mark student work. You must review its results before using or sharing them.</li>
          <li>Grading requires an internet connection and your permission to send pages through our server to Google.</li>
          <li>Our server does not save your pages or grading results, except in a problem report you choose to send. Saved work is held on your device; Google's handling is explained in the Privacy Policy.</li>
          <li>Grading uses units. A marked page costs 5 to 20 units at Brief output, by how much grading work it takes, and 5 or 10 more at Detailed; a context page costs 3. Requests that return no graded work or reach the response length limit are not charged.</li>
          <li>Subscriptions renew automatically until canceled through Apple. Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription.</li>
          <li>These Terms preserve any consumer rights that the law does not allow us to exclude.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>This section is a summary. If it differs from the detailed sections below, those sections apply.</p>
        <h2 id="s3">3. Words used in these Terms</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>App</strong>: Matdo Grade, including updates made available through the App Store.</li>
          <li><strong>Service</strong>: our server-based grading service, which sends requests to the AI provider and returns results.</li>
          <li><strong>Student Work</strong>: pages you submit, anything written on them, and the grades, annotations and feedback produced from them.</li>
          <li><strong>Output</strong>: AI-generated marks, answers, worked solutions, rubric results and feedback.</li>
          <li><strong>Device</strong>: an iPhone or iPad running the App.</li>
          <li><strong>Output Level</strong>: Brief or Detailed. Brief gives marks, answers and a short working check; Detailed adds worked solutions and notes on errors.</li>
          <li><strong>Unit</strong>: the measure used to charge for grading, explained in section 12.</li>
          <li><strong>Allowance</strong>: the Units available under a Subscription for one monthly period, as described in section 12.</li>
