          <li><strong>Apple</strong>: Apple Inc. and its subsidiaries that distribute the App and process App Store purchases.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 id="s4">4. What the App does</h2>
        <p>The App captures pages, sends them for grading and displays marks on the page. It can provide worked solutions and, in Essay Mode, feedback based on a rubric. Captured pages and results are saved on your Device and can be exported as images.</p>
        <p>The App assists teachers, tutors and parents with marking. It is not an examination or assessment authority and does not replace professional judgment.</p>
        <p>Matdo Grade is an independent product. Its use of Google and Apple services does not mean they endorse it. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by any school, examination board, curriculum authority or franchise brand. Third-party trademarks belong to their owners.</p>
        <h2 id="s5">5. Reviewing AI results</h2>
        <p>AI can misread handwriting, misunderstand a question, use an unsuitable method, produce an incorrect answer or invent information. The App checks for some errors, but it cannot detect every mistake. A confident-looking result may still be wrong.</p>
        <p>Treat every Output as a draft. Check it before returning work to a student, entering a grade, reporting to a parent or making a decision about a student.</p>
        <p>Do not use the Output as the sole basis for an official grade, placement, report card, qualification, disciplinary finding, academic-integrity finding or other decision that materially affects a person. You remain responsible for reviewing the result and exercising your own judgment.</p>
        <p>We do not guarantee that the Output is accurate, complete, appropriate for teaching or suitable for your curriculum. Our responsibility for losses is subject to sections 18 and 19 and any rights that cannot legally be excluded.</p>
        <h2 id="s6">6. Apple and the App Store</h2>
        <p>The App is licensed under Apple's standard Licensed Application End User License Agreement (Apple EULA), available at <a href="https://apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/" rel="noopener">apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/</a>. These Terms supplement that agreement. If they conflict with the Apple EULA or the App Store terms applicable to your purchase, the applicable Apple terms take precedence to the extent of the conflict. Your mandatory consumer rights remain protected.</p>
        <p>These Terms are between you and us. Apple is not a party and does not have to provide support or maintenance. We are responsible for App-related claims, including product liability, regulatory and consumer claims, and for handling third-party intellectual-property claims about the App.</p>
        <p>If the App fails to meet an applicable warranty, you may notify Apple, which will refund the purchase price paid for the App. Apple has no further warranty obligations to the extent permitted by law; we remain responsible for other warranty claims and remedies required by law. Refunds for Subscriptions and Top-Ups are addressed in section 15.</p>
        <p>You confirm that you are not in a country subject to a U.S. government embargo or designated as supporting terrorism, and are not on a U.S. prohibited or restricted-party list. You must comply with applicable export laws.</p>
        <p>Apple and its subsidiaries are third-party beneficiaries of these Terms and may enforce them.</p>
        <h2 id="s7">7. Your license to use the App</h2>
        <p>We grant you a personal, nonexclusive, nontransferable license to use the App on Apple-branded devices you own or control, subject to these Terms and the App Store Usage Rules. This gives you permission to use the App; it does not transfer ownership. Your license may be suspended or ended as described in section 21.</p>
        <p>Subscriptions and balances are associated with one Apple Account and shared across its devices when the App can verify the App Store identifier. An organization using several Apple Accounts needs separate purchases for each. Subscriptions and Top-Ups are not shared through Family Sharing.</p>
        <h2 id="s8">8. Internet access and AI providers</h2>
        <p>Grading takes place through the Service, using Google's Gemini model on Vertex AI. The App cannot grade without a working internet connection, although saved work remains available offline. You are responsible for any internet or mobile-data charges.</p>
        <p>Grading also depends on the AI provider. Outages, delays and changes to its models may affect availability and results. We may change a model or provider to maintain or improve the Service. We will update the Privacy Policy and obtain renewed permission where required before changing how or with whom grading information is shared.</p>
        <h2 id="s9">9. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may use the App to grade work in your role as a teacher, tutor, parent or an equivalent role. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Upload material you do not have the right or permission to share with us and the AI provider.</li>
          <li>Use AI grading where a student has been promised human-only marking without first correcting that understanding and obtaining any required permission.</li>
