          <li>Use the Service or Output to develop a product or service similar to or competing with Google's AI/ML services, replace or bypass a Google model, or build or improve a similar model, except through a feature that Google expressly permits under its applicable terms.</li>
          <li>Automate requests, submit work at volumes beyond ordinary classroom use, or use the App as a general interface to the AI model.</li>
          <li>Remove ownership notices, interfere with the Service or use it unlawfully.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your use must also comply with Google's Generative AI Prohibited Use Policy at <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms/generative-ai/use-policy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/terms/generative-ai/use-policy</a>, including its restrictions on harmful content, misuse of personal information and deceptive uses of AI.</p>
        <p>We may apply limits to protect the Service, including daily account and service-wide limits. A request declined because of a limit is not charged. Daily limits reset at midnight UTC. A Subscription provides an Allowance, not unlimited access or an exemption from these limits.</p>
        <h2 id="s10">10. Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p>Before submitting Student Work, check that AI grading and sharing with the providers described in the Privacy Policy are allowed by your school's policies, your employer, applicable law and any parent or student agreement. Obtain any required approval, notice or consent. We do not assess those requirements for you or guarantee that the App meets them.</p>
        <p>Review every Output as required by section 5. Protect your Device with a passcode, keep its software current and control access to saved student information.</p>
        <p>Maintain any records you need, including appropriate backups or exports. Our server does not keep your pages or results and cannot restore them. You are responsible for choosing suitable recipients and services when sharing exported work.</p>
        <h2 id="s11">11. Student Work and privacy</h2>
        <p>You or your organization decide which Student Work to submit and must have authority to share it. We process submitted pages to provide the grading you request. Our server does not save page images, rubrics, answers, grades or feedback, except in a problem report you choose to send, and we do not use Student Work to train AI models.</p>
        <p>The Privacy Policy explains Google's processing, the identifiers and operational records we keep, retention and your choices. Your permission in the App covers grading uploads; it does not replace school approval or any legally required parent or student permission.</p>
        <p>These Terms and the Privacy Policy do not, by themselves, establish compliance with student privacy laws or replace a required school data-processing agreement. Contact us before submitting work if your organization needs an agreement or restrictions on processing locations.</p>
        <h2 id="s12">12. Units and the free grant</h2>
        <p>A page that receives marks costs 5, 10, 15 or 20 Units at Brief output, depending on how much grading work the page takes. That is measured by the length of the grading response for the page, as reported by the AI provider, with the number of questions on the page deciding a page close to a boundary and capping the charge for an unusually long response. Detailed output adds 5 Units to a 5- or 10-Unit page and 10 Units to a 15- or 20-Unit page, so a marked page costs 10 to 30 Units at Detailed. A context page that the model reads to grade other work costs 3 Units at either level. You can mark context pages before grading. Settings shows your balance. Page estimates assume a typical marked page at Brief output, 10 Units.</p>
        <p>Charges are calculated after a result is returned, based on the work graded. A request that returns no graded work, or a response cut off by the Service's length limit, costs no Units. A regrade is a new request and may be charged again, including when you change the Output Level or switch between Worksheet and Essay Mode.</p>
        <p>Before grading, the App checks that your balance can cover every submitted page you did not mark as context as a marked page at the lowest price for the chosen Output Level: 5 Units at Brief, 10 at Detailed. If it cannot, the request does not start, even if the eventual charge might have been lower. If the eventual charge is more than your remaining balance, we take only what remains and do not charge the rest.</p>
        <p>The standard one-time free grant is 100 Units, about ten marked pages at Brief output. It does not renew each month. Where the App Store identifier is available, it is granted once per Apple Account. Testing or promotional grants may differ; the App shows the balance available to you. Once the grant is spent, further grading requires a Subscription or Top-Up when purchases are available. Saved work, exports and the rubric editor remain usable with an empty balance.</p>
        <p>We may change grading costs or future free grants with notice of material changes. Changes will not alter charges for completed requests or reduce the number of Units you have already bought. A change in grading cost may affect how many pages those Units can cover.</p>
        <h2 id="s13">13. Subscriptions, Top-Ups and cancellation</h2>
        <p>Our monthly plans provide the following Allowances. The listed prices are in U.S. dollars; section 14 explains which purchase price applies.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Lite</strong>: 750 Units per month, $4.99 per month.</li>
          <li><strong>Plus</strong>: 2,000 Units per month, $9.99 per month.</li>
          <li><strong>Pro</strong>: 4,500 Units per month, $19.99 per month.</li>
          <li><strong>Max</strong>: 10,000 Units per month, $39.99 per month.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>At Brief output, these Allowances cover about 75, 200, 450 or 1,000 typical marked pages; lighter pages cost fewer Units and longer pages more. Detailed output uses 5 or 10 more Units per marked page. Context pages cost fewer Units. The Unit Allowance, rather than a page estimate, determines your balance. No plan is unlimited. Purchases may be unavailable during testing.</p>
        <p>While your Subscription is active, its Allowance resets each month at 12:01 a.m. in your device's time zone, on the same day of the month your Subscription started. If a month has no such day, it resets on that month's last day. Settings shows the date and time of the next reset. Unused monthly Units expire at the reset and do not normally carry forward. The free grant is one-time and does not reset.</p>
        <p>If you upgrade during a monthly period, the unused Allowance from the previous plan is carried into the upgraded balance until the next reset. These carried Units expire at that reset. When a Subscription ends, its Allowance and any carried Units are no longer available.</p>
        <p>A Top-Up currently provides 1,000 Units for $6.99. It is a one-time purchase and does not renew. Top-Up Units do not expire and can be used without an active Subscription. They are used after the monthly Allowance or free grant and any carried Units. Spent Units are not automatically restored; refund requests and mandatory consumer rights are covered in section 15.</p>
        <p>Apple charges your Apple Account when you confirm a purchase. Subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled at least 24 hours before the current billing period ends. Apple may charge for renewal during the 24 hours before that period ends.</p>
        <p>You can manage or cancel through the App's Settings or through your Device's Settings → your name → Subscriptions. Cancellation stops future renewals; you normally retain access until the paid period ends. Upgrades take effect immediately and downgrades at the next renewal, subject to Apple's purchase terms. Deleting the App or requesting deletion of your balance does not cancel a Subscription.</p>
        <p>If a subscription free trial is offered, its terms are shown before you accept it. Any unused trial period may be forfeited when you purchase a Subscription, as explained in the offer. The one-time free Unit grant is separate from a subscription trial.</p>
        <h2 id="s14">14. Prices and taxes</h2>
        <p>The App Store shows the price and currency that apply before you confirm a purchase. That price takes precedence over the example U.S. prices in these Terms. Taxes are included or added according to the rules for your App Store region, and Apple collects them where required.</p>
        <p>We may change prices for future purchases. Price increases for an existing Subscription follow Apple's notice and consent rules. Where your consent is required and you do not give it, the Subscription will not renew at the increased price.</p>
        <h2 id="s15">15. Refunds and billing problems</h2>
        <p>Apple processes App Store payments and refund requests. To request a refund, visit <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com" rel="noopener">reportaproblem.apple.com</a> or contact Apple Support. We cannot directly issue, approve or decline an App Store refund. Apple applies its refund policies and any consumer rights required by law.</p>
        <p>A refunded Subscription no longer entitles you to its Allowance. Refunds may affect the associated purchase entitlement or Unit balance. Nothing in these Terms removes a right to a refund or other remedy that applicable law gives you.</p>
        <p>If grading fails, you believe a charge is incorrect or the App is defective, contact <a href="mailto:matdo@matdolab.com">matdo@matdolab.com</a>. We can investigate Service and Unit-accounting issues separately from Apple's payment refund process.</p>
        <h2 id="s16">16. Availability, updates and support</h2>
        <p>We may update the App and change its features or grading models. Your Device settings control automatic installation of updates. We cannot promise uninterrupted grading or a fixed response time, because the Service depends on internet access and third-party providers.</p>
        <p>We may stop offering the App, the Service or support for an operating-system version. We will give reasonable notice where practicable and honor any obligations and remedies required by law for purchases already made.</p>
        <p>For support, contact <a href="mailto:matdo@matdolab.com">matdo@matdolab.com</a>. We aim to respond promptly, but do not promise a particular response time or service level. Apple is not responsible for App support.</p>
        <h2 id="s17">17. Ownership and feedback</h2>
        <p>We own the App's code, design, interface, grading prompts, and Matdo and Matdo Grade branding, except for third-party materials and components, which remain subject to their owners' rights and licenses. Your license permits use of the App; it does not transfer these rights.</p>
        <p>We claim no ownership of Student Work. You grant us only the permission needed to process submitted work and return the Output, and to keep and review a problem report you send, as described in these Terms and the Privacy Policy. As between you and us, you may use, keep and share the Output, subject to section 9 and the rights of students and other third parties. Output may resemble results given to others. We do not promise that it is unique or that copyright protection is available.</p>
        <p>If you send a suggestion or product feedback, you allow us to use it without payment or an obligation to adopt it. Do not include confidential information or student work in product feedback, except in a problem report sent with Report issue in the App. For support, avoid sending student work or sensitive information unless needed to resolve the issue, as explained in the Privacy Policy.</p>
