        <p>To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary or punitive damages arising from the App, Service or these Terms. This includes lost profits, business or goodwill, lost or corrupted records, incorrect grades or feedback, and decisions based on the Output, to the extent the law permits their exclusion.</p>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, our total liability for claims relating to the App, Service or these Terms is limited to the greater of US$100 or the total amount you have paid for the App, Subscriptions and Top-Ups. This limit applies across all such claims, whether based on contract, negligence or another legal ground, even if we were told a loss might occur or a limited remedy does not achieve its purpose.</p>
        <p>These limits do not apply to death or personal injury caused by negligence, fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation, or any other liability that cannot legally be excluded or limited. Where local law prohibits a particular exclusion or limit, it does not apply to you.</p>
        <h2 id="s20">20. Claims arising from misuse</h2>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, you agree to reimburse and protect Matdo Lab LLC against third-party claims, losses and reasonable legal expenses resulting from your breach of these Terms, submission of work without the required authority or permission, or use of the Output in breach of section 5. This is sometimes called an indemnity.</p>
        <p>This obligation does not cover losses caused by our own breach of these Terms, negligence or unlawful conduct, and does not override your mandatory consumer rights. We will give you reasonable notice of a claim, allow you to participate in its defense and take reasonable steps to limit the loss. We will not agree to a settlement that imposes obligations on you without your consent, which must not be unreasonably withheld.</p>
        <h2 id="s21">21. Ending use or access</h2>
        <p>These Terms apply while you use the App or Service. You may stop using them at any time. To end your use, cancel any Subscription through Apple and delete the App from your Devices. Export any saved work you need first. Deleting the App does not cancel purchases or remove server records and backups; the Privacy Policy explains deletion options.</p>
